---
/**
 * The outcome legend plus the "How to read these bars" disclosure (plan §4:
 * explanations behind a disclosure), above a list of fixtures.
 */
---

<div class="head">
  <ul class="legend" aria-label="Colours">
    <li><i style="background: var(--home)"></i>Home win</li>
    <li><i style="background: var(--draw)"></i>Draw</li>
    <li><i style="background: var(--away)"></i>Away win</li>
  </ul>
  <details class="how">
    <summary>How to read these bars</summary>
    <p>
      Each bar splits 100% between a home win, a draw and an away win. The solid segment is the model's pick: the most
      likely of the three. Once a match is played, the outcome that happened is outlined. Tap a match for the team
      ratings behind it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The ratings are Elo ratings built from results and recent expected goals (xG). The gap includes home advantage.
    </p>
  </details>
</div>

<style>
  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px 16px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px 16px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .legend li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .legend i {
    display: block;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .how {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .how summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .how p {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 6px 0 0;
  }

  .how[open] {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }
</style>
